   342	  timing views, plan 1.7) at both operating points, plus **C2 at 4410 only**
   343	  (the §6 comparator point; a C2 trace at 352800 is not budgeted);
   344	  profiling-perturbation runs (A, C3, G: one matching block each,
   345	  unprofiled vs `--cuda-graph-trace=graph` vs `=node`, reduced to ratios
   346	  with the >5 % caveat flag by `fullmodel/perturbation.py`);
   347	  attention-backend microbench (plan 1.5: time-axis batch 60 × seq T and
   348	  freq-axis batch T × seq 60, heads 8, dim_head 64, fp16, default scale,
   349	  dropout 0; TWO layout families — the model's actual SDPA input layouts
   350	  read from the C3 generated code (q/k as (b,n,h,d)-contiguous rotary
   351	  outputs viewed as (b,h,n,d); v a strided view into the fused qkv output)
   352	  and, as a separate experiment, contiguous (b,h,n,d); flash / efficient /
   353	  cuDNN / math forced one at a time, fp32 MATH-forced reference, CUDA-graph-
   354	  replayed device timing, unsupported cases recorded; the model's deployed
   355	  backend established PER operating point AND axis from the C3 node traces
   356	  — the 12 attention executions per pass in (time, freq) × 6 order, Triton
   357	  preprocessing kernels excluded — and a case whose deployed backend is not
   358	  established from a trace has NO ratio and is UNRESOLVED, never assumed);
   359	  boundary microbench (§4) plus its node-level trace and traced-vs-unprofiled
   360	  perturbation; per-kernel ideal costs (plan 1.4) computed only from the
   361	  compiled variant(s) whose ORDERED per-pass Triton sequence is reproduced
   362	  by a UNIQUE decomposition into compiled-graph call sequences (graphs may
   363	  repeat; graphs with identical kernel sequences and call signatures are one
   364	  interchangeable class; graphs without Triton kernels are invisible to the
   365	  decomposition and are stated as such; SDPA call count reconciled exactly,
   366	  GEMM events ≥ extern calls, captured pass count = 50; zero or several
   367	  decompositions → UNRESOLVED, expected for graph-broken arms such as C1/C2
   368	  whose per-graph kernel numbering makes names non-unique). Inductor GEMM
   369	  template kernels (`triton_tem_*`, max-autotune) are counted in the GEMM
   370	  class and are not priced by the byte model. Registered deviations from a literal
   371	  per-kernel FLOPs/bytes table: cuBLAS kernel names carry no shapes, so GEMM
   372	  ideals are computed per extern call site from the wrapper and compared at
   373	  class level; SDPA ideals are class-level (12 calls/pass at the model
   374	  shapes); Inductor fused pointwise/reduction kernels are priced by bytes
   375	  only (bandwidth bound, zero FLOPs) with per-call L2 residency tests. Byte
   376	  model for a fused kernel call: per pointer argument, element size from the
   377	  kernel's own ABI signature (`triton_meta`), traffic = min(distinct
   378	  elements of the argument's strided footprint, load/store sites × the
   379	  call's iteration space) × element size, reads and writes charged
   380	  separately; graph-input dtypes from the wrapper's benchmark section;
   381	  fallback-op outputs from their `assert_size_stride`. This over-counts
   382	  slice reads, so a row whose HBM-model ideal exceeds its measured time is
   383	  flagged `bound_not_tight` and its recoverable share under the HBM model is
   384	  0 (never negative, never inflated); eager ATen fallbacks, cuFFT and copy
   385	  kernels without wrapper shapes stay UNRESOLVED. A kernel → fused-op source
   386	  map with its coverage share accompanies the table; exports; evidence
   387	  extraction. Session 2 runs under the
   388	  same deadline/reserve/terminal-record rules as session 1 (qualification
   389	  and microbenchmarks included).
   390	  **Plan 1.7 dependency model (registered):** the exports carry no event or
   391	  graph edges, so the critical-path view is the OBSERVED-ORDER longest chain
   392	  of pairwise non-overlapping kernels (edge a→b iff a ended before b
   393	  started); it is an upper bound on the true dependency path, satisfies
   394	  `critical_path ≤ union ≤ span` by construction (asserted), and is labelled
   395	  as such; the union and the summed views are exact.
   396	- Engineering shakedown of the harness on ml-beast GPU 4 is permitted before
   397	  session 1 (the `sm120` smoke rule): its outputs are never session evidence
   398	  and are never cited.
   399	- Budget guard: every process runs under `timeout`; a timed-out or crashed
   400	  run is INVALID/UNTESTED in its JSON and the session continues (loud in the
   401	  console log, never silent).
