     1	# Plan — agent-first ceiling ledger for MelBandRoformer on RTX 5090
     2	### v0.1 · 2026-09-16 · owner: Muhit · executors: coding agents (Phases 1–2), owner (Phase 3+)
     3	
     4	**Purpose.** Agents run the corrected measurement session and then compute, for every candidate
     5	optimization X, its ceiling Y — "if X were done perfectly, it is worth Y ms (Z%) at operating
     6	point O" — with the formula, the measured inputs, the assumptions, a confidence label, an effort
     7	class, and the closest prior work. The owner reads one table, picks the X's whose Y is impressive,
     8	audits those rows, and dives only there. Nothing is implemented before its ceiling is known.
     9	
    10	This is a what-if analysis in the Daydream/Habitat lineage (Pekhimenko group), applied to compiled
    11	inference on consumer GPUs. As a *planning instrument* it is exactly right. As a *paper* it would
    12	be judged against that lineage — so every ceiling is a registered prediction, and Phase 3
    13	interventions score it. The scored ledger is the evidence base; whether it becomes a paper is
    14	decided afterwards (reviewer's Q3), not assumed.
    15	
    16	Three questions, in order (adopted verbatim from the external review):
    17	1. Does an optimization give a meaningful, reproducible benefit? (engineering)
    18	2. Can the benefit or its absence be explained without confounded attribution? (mechanism)
    19	3. Does the explanation add knowledge beyond the closest prior work? (publication)
    20	Phases 1–3 answer Q1 and produce the inputs for Q2. Q3 is a separate decision at week 8.
