   292	  three matched restarts) under one manifest with one variant pair and both
   293	  arms' cells hold that SDR qualification; the matched runner re-checks each
   294	  arm's recording state after the joint settle and after validation.
   295	  **Recording observer:** compiled runs snapshot the cudagraph-trees
   296	  manager's recorded graph nodes (roots and descendants) together with the
   297	  dynamo/inductor counters at every phase boundary; a missing observer
   298	  leaves stability UNRESOLVED and the run ineligible.
   299	  **Runtime pins and manifest scope:** every process checks torch ==
   300	  2.8.0+cu128 and triton == 3.4.0 before building; the manifest binds the
   301	  complete measuring set (fullmodel/**, arms/*, scripts/*, configs/*,
   302	  frontend.py, frontend_rms_fused.py, setup.sh, this registration, the
   303	  runtime identity) and is compared field by field on every load; every
   304	  reference artifact (validation outputs, eager-A clip outputs) carries its
   305	  own lineage sidecar (manifest id + sha256) checked before use.
   306	- **Unprofiled timing is the primary result.** Session-2 traces are for
   307	  mechanism; profiled and unprofiled numbers never share a ratio. Profiling
   308	  perturbation (plan 1.6): A, C3, G at 4410 and 352800, wall unprofiled vs
   309	  `--cuda-graph-trace=graph` vs `=node`; >5 % inflation → every mechanism
   310	  number from that trace carries the factor as a caveat.
   311	- **Session 1 (≤ 3 h, RunPod secure-cloud RTX 5090, pod name
   312	  `melband_profiling`, image `runpod/pytorch:1.1.0-rc.154-cu1281-torch280-ubuntu2204`
   313	  = the pinned torch 2.8.0+cu128 / triton 3.4.0 matrix):** in this order —
   314	  setup (idempotent `setup.sh` + clip pack + nsys check); eager-A references
   315	  at both operating points; the two planted-fault checks; C3 operator
   316	  qualification per frame count; the matched pairs (§5, plan 1.2); the arm
   317	  matrix at 352800 and 4410 (three round-major restarts, SDR gate in r1 at
   318	  both points); C2 last. Budget guards (registered): a hard session deadline
   319	  (3 h) with a 15-min extraction reserve — a cell that cannot start before
   320	  the reserve is `UNTESTED(deadline)` and the session is INCOMPLETE, never
   321	  salvaged by weakening validation or timing; per-process caps (25 min
   322	  compile arms, 15 min others); an **aggregate C2 allowance of 40 min**, and
   323	  a timed-out cold C2 attempt is not retried at that operating point (the
   324	  remaining restarts are `UNTESTED`; a timeout means unavailable
   325	  performance, not evidence that C2 is slow). Every run's JSON carries
   326	  `headline_eligible` with machine-readable reasons; a headline per (arm ×
   327	  operating point) requires three complete eligible restarts with the same
   328	  effective variant (capture scope / adapter / compile mode), else the cell
   329	  is `INCOMPLETE`. At the end of each session `fullmodel/completeness.py`
   330	  audits the registered mandatory items and writes the mechanical session
   331	  verdict (COMPLETE / INCOMPLETE with per-item reasons) to
   332	  `session_status.json`; supervisor messages go to stderr and every bounded
   333	  auxiliary step leaves a terminal `aux_<name>.json` (OK / FAILED /
   334	  UNTESTED). Pod setup (image boot, `setup.sh`) precedes the session clock.
   335	  Evidence extraction before terminate.
   336	- **Session 2 (≤ 3 h):** eager-A references + SDR at the sweep points; chunk
