   586	def main():
     1	"""Boundary-cost microbenchmark (plan 0.4; prereg_amendments.md §4).
     2	
     3	Protocol (registered):
     4	  chains of N DEPENDENT kernels, N ∈ {10, 100, 1000, 2000}:
     5	    trivial : one Triton program loads ONE int32 element, adds 1, stores it
     6	              back to the SAME buffer -> kernel k+1 depends on kernel k; the
     7	              final counter value must equal the total number of launches
     8	              (dependency proof, exact integer arithmetic)
     9	    elem37  : in-place fp16 elementwise op on a 37 MB tensor (x.mul_(1.0)),
    10	              value-preserving, N ∈ {10, 100}
    11	    gemm    : alternating dependent GEMMs 660x384x1536 / 660x1536x384 fp16 into
    12	              PREALLOCATED ping-pong outputs (torch.matmul(out=)), weights scaled
    13	              by 1/sqrt(K) so magnitudes stay bounded, N ∈ {10, 100}
    14	  modes:
    15	    stream     : back-to-back launches on the current stream
    16	    graph      : the chain captured into one CUDA graph, replayed
    17	    pdl_stream : trivial kernels launched with programmatic dependent launch
    18	                 (Triton 3.4 `launch_pdl=True`; gdc_wait() BEFORE the dependent
    19	                 load, gdc_launch_dependents() AFTER the store); PTX checked
    20	                 for griddepcontrol instructions
    21	    pdl_graph  : the PDL chain captured into a CUDA graph
    22	    (real-kernel PDL: not available through cuBLAS/ATen launches -> UNSUPPORTED)
    23	  timing: unprofiled DEVICE time via CUDA events around the chain, median of
    24	  REPEATS, min/max; T(N) per (chain, mode); least-squares slope and intercept
    25	  over N (slope = effective per-node service time INCLUDING kernel execution;
    26	  intercept = fixed chain overhead). This script does NOT claim a pure
    27	  boundary cost: `--analyze-trace` reads the node-level trace of a separate
    28	  run of this script and reports, per chain segment (NVTX range), the median
    29	  kernel duration and the median serial inter-kernel gap; the gap is the
    30	  boundary estimate for non-PDL modes; for PDL modes kernels overlap and
    31	  no subtraction is attempted (UNRESOLVED as a pure boundary). Perturbation
    32	  of the traced run vs the unprofiled T(N) is reported.
    33	"""
