One more CPU counterexample reproduced a pricing error: a legal Triton call with a zero-offset `reinterpret_tensor` is assigned zero bytes and a 100% recoverable share. The parser multiplies every numeric literal on the call line, including the storage offset. I’m assembling the final findings and closure table.
